{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/876550-why-do-you-play","id":876550,"title":"Why do you play?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-28T06:10:09-07:00","id":876550,"title":"Why do you play?","content":"Why do you play?<br /> <br /> Not related to a specific setting, but a question in general about tabletop roleplaying games. What is it that you seek when you play, or write for a tabletop RPG? What motivates you to return to the table, be it real or virtual?<br /> <br /> I am a storyteller for Vampire: The Masquerade and run a Pathfinder campaign as well. Though they are both very different beasts I love writing because of the world you can create, the intricate little details to build and most of all, the wonder experienced by the players.<br /> It gives me a lot of satisfaction to see players struggle with the challenges I set forth and get immersed in the story. Genuine fear of loosing their character, sadness over the loss of a dear NPC or the victory rush they get when they do survive. It always amazes me to see what they come up with and how they react. That is why I play.<br /> <br /> So, why do you play tabletop RPG's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11543-arli\u00e8n","name":"Arli\u00e8n","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T06:22:12-07:00","id":876558,"title":"","content":"I play to be a part of something greater than myself. In real life I'm an atheist: I don't believe in any Great Plans or purposes. Destiny isn't fixed, I'm not the protagonist of my own story, there are millions of things that could affect my life in significant ways that I have no control over. When I suffer, it's not in service of a greater power, or leading to a revelatory climax. Most of the time, I find this relaxing, freeing. Liberating. Affirming.<br /> <br /> It's also scary. Uncertain. Gaming lets me be a part of something greater. The character I create is a part of a narrative. Their suffering comes with wisdom, and they have opportunities to do great things. I can address my real-life fears via proxy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:59:57-07:00","id":878417,"title":"","content":"I play for several reasons..<br /> 1) camraderie. Over the years keeping gaming with the same group of people, builds up friendships<br /> 2) its fun!!<br /> 3) it challenges the mind. <br /> and my fave.. #4) Its a lot cheaper compared to Some other hobbies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T10:38:25-07:00","id":879585,"title":"","content":"Cooperative storytelling. I don't know what's coming next, but I can affect what happens. When I'm watching a show or reading a novel, I often think about how I would have written things differently; I rarely get that feeling from a tabletop session for multiple subtle reasons. When I'm writing something myself, it's sometimes burdensome to decide absolutely everything that happens; tabletop gaming removes that burden by including dice and other people into the storytelling process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 05-02-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T01:25:12-07:00","id":879978,"title":"","content":"I play because my imagination has always been over-active. When I was young, I was constantly away in some day-dream. Books gave me some ability to satisfy my imagination, but eventually those stories would end and I'd be back to day-dreaming. Then video games came into my life, but they did more to inspire my imagination to soar to even greater heights than they did to sate the beast. Finally, by happenstance, I saw a book cover on a store shelf that caught my attention. It was the first role-playing game I'd ever played, or even heard of, and it gave me everything that I got from reading a novel, playing a video game, or day-dreaming, but also gave me something specifically lacking from those things: Infinite possibility for the tale to continue or start anew.<br /> <br /> If not for being able to channel my imagination into role-playing games, I'd probably be non-functional as a person.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:51:35-07:00","id":886437,"title":"","content":"Fascinating to see such diverse reasons, though that imagination does come back each time. Not all that surprising though as you need a whole lot of it to play!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11543-arli\u00e8n","name":"Arli\u00e8n","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T12:36:47-07:00","id":886557,"title":"","content":"Why do I play? Because at some point in my life, just watching/reading the stories was not enough. So, I started analyzing them. But that still wasn't enough, I wanted to make my own. But just writing it wasn't enough, I wanted a challenge, something to make it not so easy for the good guy to win. Then I found RPGs and that was exactly what I was looking for. First I played, then I got a taste of the director's chair (GM/ST/DM) and I was hooked on that.<br /> <br /> I got to play a game that was a story that made me think ahead of the players, occasionally failing to do so which forced me to think even faster, and enjoy the moment of the story and the end result with retrospection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T14:08:40-07:00","id":886630,"title":"","content":"I play for several reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) (and usually most important) To socialize/interact with close friends (or at least reasonably close acquaintances; I rarely, if ever, game with strangers nowadays -- my time is limited, so I want to spend it with people I know...)<br /> <br /> 2) To &quot;become&quot; someone/thing else other than myself (I am not necessarily a great actor, but I've been told by many of my friends that I am usually very good about &quot;getting into character&quot;, so as to behave/act like someone often very different from myself); it often provides a great deal of insight into how others think and/or process things.<br /> <br /> 3) To experiment with various settings/narratives that simply can't occur in Real Life(tm).<br /> <br /> 4) To &quot;get&quot; the &quot;feeling and flavor&quot; of a particular game setting, genre or milieu; DnD, even when run differently by different people, has an unmistakably &quot;flavor/feel&quot; to it (as most of us know), and that's fun... but so is experiencing the different realities conveyed in other settings (both by dint of fluff as well as by those conveyed by the game mechanics, which become a &quot;language&quot; all unto themselves).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I usually always have fun in various ways during all of that, so I rarely ever list it as a separate component....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T04:09:03-07:00","id":887067,"title":"","content":"Well, Papa Bear and I share motivation and cause. So, what he said.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T04:44:17-07:00","id":887076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/876550-why-do-you-play?p=886630#post886630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually always have fun in various ways during all of that, so I rarely ever list it as a separate component....</div> </div> </div> </div>To play without having fun seems more suitable for a Vampire character's motivation. I will take a wild guess and assume everyone intents to have fun when playing a hobby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11543-arli\u00e8n","name":"Arli\u00e8n","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T10:53:41-07:00","id":887297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arli\u00e8n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/876550-why-do-you-play?p=887076#post887076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To play without having fun seems more suitable for a Vampire character's motivation. I will take a wild guess and assume everyone intents to have fun when playing a hobby.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I was citing that as a specific point because some people -- when posed with a question like the one in this thread -- give &quot;to have fun&quot; as a listed reason for playing an RPG; my point was to indicate that I, too, thought that was a given/inherent to the hobby, so it need not be listed (as some people do). (Also, it was to clarify, by relation, that there have been occasions where I played in a game -- one session or several -- wherein I wasn't having fun, as such, in terms of the game in-and-of-itself, but it was fine because I was hanging out with friends, so I just &quot;went with the flow&quot;, as it were. &gt;shrugs&lt; )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:43:05-07:00","id":887507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/876550-why-do-you-play?p=886557#post886557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do I play? Because at some point in my life, just watching/reading the stories was not enough. So, I started analyzing them. But that still wasn't enough, I wanted to make my own. But just writing it wasn't enough, I wanted a challenge, something to make it not so easy for the good guy to win. Then I found RPGs and that was exactly what I was looking for. First I played, then I got a taste of the director's chair (GM/ST/DM) and I was hooked on that..</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the GM's i game with in Starwars at conventions was like that. He got tired of just reading all the SW novels, and wanted to become more involved..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}